MyVpn — third-party notices and provenance
==========================================

MyVpn is an independent implementation that *may* incorporate code adapted from prior
art in the Xray/V2Ray client ecosystem. Every adapted component is recorded, with its
upstream file and the nature of the change, in `docs/provenance.md`; that register is the
authoritative record and this file summarises it.

The distinction that matters is between "studied" and "derived". Studied influence is
recorded in `docs/adr/` and `docs/research/`. Derived code is recorded in the register
and carries an attribution header in the file itself. As of this revision **no component
has been adapted from another client** — the register contains no entries — but the
policy below governs what may be, and what must never be.

That register also carries a **do-not-copy list**: components whose upstream
implementation is defective in a way this project was created to fix. Those are excluded
regardless of convenience, because copying them would silently reintroduce the exact
defects the project exists to eliminate.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Xray-core (the network engine)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Project : https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-core
License : Mozilla Public License 2.0 (MPL-2.0)

MyVpn does NOT link against or modify Xray-core source code. It launches the
Xray-core binary as a separate process and communicates with it through a
generated JSON configuration file and its process stdout/stderr. The Xray-core
binary is distributed unmodified, either:

  * fetched from the official release channel with SHA-256 verification, or
  * supplied by the user as a system package / manual binary selection.

MPL-2.0 is a file-level copyleft licence. Because Xray-core is consumed as a
separate executable and never as linked source, MPL-2.0 imposes no licensing
obligation on MyVpn's own source code. The unmodified Xray-core binary, and any
license/notice files shipped alongside it, remain under MPL-2.0. When MyVpn
bundles Xray-core (in installer/portable/AppImage artifacts), the upstream
LICENSE file is redistributed verbatim in the bundle's `licenses/` directory.

