3. Reference projects studied (NO code copied)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Project : v2rayN — https://github.com/2dust/v2rayN
License : GPL-3.0-ONLY. Its LICENSE file is the bare GPLv3 text with no "or later"
          clause, and GitHub reports the SPDX identifier as `GPL-3.0`. Verified against
          the primary source rather than assumed.
Use     : Two distinct relationships, which must not be conflated:

          (a) STUDIED. Architecture, UX and failure-mode analysis, recorded in
              docs/research/01-v2rayn-architecture.md and the ADRs. This is not a
              licensing event.

          (b) ADAPTED. Code may be adapted from v2rayN. This is permitted because
              GPL-3.0-only and GPL-3.0-or-later are compatible licences: the combined
              work may be distributed under GPL-3.0. The obligations that follow are
              not optional:
                * preserve the upstream copyright notice and licence text;
                * mark modified files as modified, with the date of change;
                * state the nature of the change;
                * make the complete corresponding source available (it is);
                * impose no further restrictions on the adapted parts.

          Because the additional "or later" permission cannot be granted over someone
          else's GPL-3.0-only code, the combined distribution is offered under
          GPL-3.0-only. See `PackageLicenseExpression` in Directory.Build.props.

          Several upstream components are on the do-not-copy list in
          docs/provenance.md — notably the core launch/environment path, which is the
          direct cause of issue #9765, the unescaped shell-script generation that runs
          as root, the absent core supervision, and the updater that verifies nothing.
          Adapting those would reintroduce the defects this project exists to fix.

Project : sing-box — https://github.com/SagerNet/sing-box
License : GNU GPL-3.0 / other
Use     : NOT USED. sing-box is explicitly excluded as a network core by the
          project requirements. It was not studied for implementation reuse.

Project : Wintun — https://www.wintun.net/ (WireGuard project)
License : GPL-2.0 / MIT dual (see upstream; the driver is distributed under a
          prebuilt-binary licence that permits redistribution of the *unmodified*
          binary, not modification)
Use     : Referenced as the Windows TUN driver. MyVpn relies on whatever TUN
          driver Xray-core itself uses on Windows and does not redistribute or
          modify a driver unless a licence review (docs/research/06) confirms it
          is permitted.

Project : Happ — https://www.happ.su/main/dev-docs
License : Proprietary application; documentation is public.
Use     : Only *publicly documented* subscription HTTP header formats are
          implemented, from the published developer documentation. No Happ code
          was copied or decompiled. See docs/research/05.

